        <body>
            <div xml:id="d123">

                <pb facs="0284" n="196" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv02/pg196"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">763.72119/2730</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Swiss Minister</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Sulzer</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 292</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1918-11-29">November 29,
                            1918</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the
                    receipt of your note dated the 16th instant regarding the evacuation of the
                    territory of Austria-Hungary by German troops within the period fixed by the
                    terms of the armistice and to inform you that the substance of the communication
                    from the Government of German Austria therein contained has been brought to the
                    attention of the competent authorities of this Government. I beg to state,
                    however, that this communication was received after the expiration of the period
                    fixed by the terms of the armistice for the evacuation of the territory of
                    Austria by German troops; namely, the 17th instant.</p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
